<title>CANADA: Spar to benefit from Canada space project.</title>
<headline>Spar to benefit from Canada space project.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian government said on Tuesday it would invest C$207 million over the next three years to develop a space robot called the Canada Hand.</p>
<p>Spar Aerospace Ltd will benefit most from the government grant, company spokeswoman Deborah Allan told Reuters.</p>
<p>She said Spar was still negotiating the precise terms with the federal government, but Spar will develop and build the Canada Hand and likely receive about C$150 million of the grant.</p>
<p>&quot;We are very excited,&quot; she said.</p>
</text>
